# Its id leads with aspect-: a State of the same name (Raging, Mindful, God Ki) has the bare one.
id: aspect-graded
name: Graded
polarity: positive
# number: its script is the whole of it. moment: entering, leaving, the start of a turn (stages 4-5).
# rule: how a Transformation is entered, left or Mastered - asked by transformations.mjs aspectLevel.
group: rule
# Its Transformation's own: it does nothing to the character in general - shown on its row, not among the Active Aspects (the user's).
bar: false
# The rule in short, for its hovers; its own words below (the page the user gave, 2026-11-20).
summary: >
  It has Grades; the Transformation Maneuver enters it in another Grade, with that Grade's Stress Test.
text: >
  Graded: You can draw additional power out of this Transformation.
  –Effect: This Transformation has Grades (see — Stages and Grades). While in a Transformation with the Graded Aspect, you may use the Transformation Maneuver to attempt to enter that same Transformation (but at a different Grade). If you do, you must still make the Stress Test for that Transformation at that Grade and if you fail, you will suffer the typical consequences.

---

# Nothing it does by itself yet: the Transformation Maneuver and Mastery read it.
